      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART I — ANCIENT INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Kalinga War (261 BCE) transformed Ashoka's governance, leading him to embrace Buddhism and adopt the policy of Dhamma.",
        "The Second Battle of Tarain (1192) laid the foundation for the Delhi Sultanate after Muhammad Ghori defeated Prithviraj Chauhan.",
        "Babur established the Mughal Empire by defeating Ibrahim Lodi in the First Battle of Panipat (1526) using artillery and Tulughma tactics.",
        "The Battle of Plassey (1757) marked the beginning of British political control in India, which was later consolidated at Buxar (1764)."
      ],
      "id": "z3f5a8q"
    },
